IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc13-logic`

-- ccc13-animals.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), Part XI: sections 444 to 447.1 (animals, cruelty to animals, cetaceans, orders of prohibition or restitution).
-- Reading of the answers as in ccc13-fraud.l4. Penalties that state a fine and a term for the summary limb (445(2)(b), 445.01(2)(b), 445.1(2)(b), 447(2)(b), 445.2(5)) are encoded; the rest use the s 787(1) input.
-- Dates are `Date day month year`. Section 445.2 turns on "the day on which this subsection comes into force", which the text does not give: it is a Date input.

§ `Part XI -- sections 444 to 447.1`

§§ `Animals -- sections 444 to 445.01`

-- src:7784 | Animals
-- src:7785 | 444 [Repealed, 2018, c. 29, s. 52]
@ref s 444 (src:7784-7785)
`s 444 as the text shows it` MEANS "444 [Repealed, 2018, c. 29, s. 52]"

-- 445 (1) Every one commits an offence who, wilfully and without lawful excuse, (a) kills, maims, wounds, poisons or injures dogs, birds or animals that are kept for a lawful purpose; or (b) places poison in such a position that it may easily be consumed by dogs, birds or animals that are kept for a lawful purpose.
-- src:7786 | Injuring or endangering other animals
-- src:7787 | 445 (1) Every one commits an offence who, wilfully and without lawful excuse,
-- src:7788 | (a) kills, maims, wounds, poisons or injures dogs, birds or animals that are kept for a lawful purpose; or
-- src:7789 | (b) places poison in such a position that it may easily be consumed by dogs, birds or animals that are kept for a lawful purpose.
@ref s 445(1) (src:7786-7789)
GIVEN `the person acts wilfully` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acts without lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person kills, maims, wounds, poisons or injures dogs, birds or animals` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person places poison in such a position that it may easily be consumed by dogs, birds or animals` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the dogs, birds or animals are kept for a lawful purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 445(1) the conduct is the offence of injuring or endangering other animals` MEANS
    IF    `the person acts wilfully`
      AND `the person acts without lawful excuse`
      AND (`the person kills, maims, wounds, poisons or injures dogs, birds or animals` OR `the person places poison in such a position that it may easily be consumed by dogs, birds or animals`)   -- (a), (b)
      AND `the dogs, birds or animals are kept for a lawful purpose`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every one commits an offence who, wilfully and without lawful excuse,"

-- src:7790 | Punishment
-- src:7791 | (2) Every one who commits an offence under subsection (1) is guilty of
-- src:7792 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than five years; or
-- src:7793 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction and liable to a fine of not more than $10,000 or to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years less a day, or to both.
@ref s 445(2) (the punishments) (src:7790-7793)
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 445(2) the punishments` MEANS LIST
    (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `five years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)   -- limb 1: the limb the text states
    , (Punishment OF `on summary conviction`, `imprisonment for a term of` `two years less a day`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `a fine of` 10000, `no fine is stated`)   -- limb 2: the limb the text states

@ref s 445(2) (the class of the offence) (src:7790-7793)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 445(2) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

-- src:7802 | Definitions
-- src:7803 | (4) The following definitions apply in this section.
-- src:7804 | law enforcement animal means a dog or horse that is trained to aid a law enforcement officer in carrying out that officer’s duties. (animal d’assistance policière)
@ref s 445.01(4) "law enforcement animal" (src:7802-7804)
GIVEN `it is a dog or horse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is trained to aid a law enforcement officer in carrying out that officer’s duties` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 445.01(4) the animal is a law enforcement animal` MEANS
    IF `it is a dog or horse` AND `it is trained to aid a law enforcement officer in carrying out that officer’s duties`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "law enforcement animal means a dog or horse that is trained to aid a law enforcement officer in carrying out that officer’s duties"

-- law enforcement officer means a police officer, a police constable or any person referred to in paragraph (b), (c.1), (d), (d.1), (e) or (g) of the definition peace officer in section 2.
-- The keel's `s 2 peace officer` answers whether a person is a peace officer, not by which paragraph: whether the person is one of the paragraphs listed is a fact the person states (a seam PLAN.md lacks: see NOTES.md, Seams).
-- src:7805 | law enforcement officer means a police officer, a police constable or any person referred to in paragraph (b), (c.1), (d), (d.1), (e) or (g) of the definition peace officer in section 2. (agent de contrôle d’application de la loi)
@ref s 445.01(4) "law enforcement officer" (src:7805-7805)
GIVEN `the person is a police officer or a police constable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is referred to in paragraph (b), (c.1), (d), (d.1), (e) or (g) of the definition peace officer in section 2` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 445.01(4) the person is a law enforcement officer` MEANS
    IF `the person is a police officer or a police constable` OR `the person is referred to in paragraph (b), (c.1), (d), (d.1), (e) or (g) of the definition peace officer in section 2`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "law enforcement officer means a police officer, a police constable or any person referred to in paragraph (b), (c.1), (d), (d.1), (e) or (g) of the definition peace officer in section 2"

-- src:7806 | military animal means an animal that is trained to aid a member of the Canadian Forces in carrying out that member’s duties. (animal d’assistance militaire)
@ref s 445.01(4) "military animal" (src:7806-7806)
GIVEN `it is an animal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is trained to aid a member of the Canadian Forces in carrying out that member’s duties` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 445.01(4) the animal is a military animal` MEANS
    IF `it is an animal` AND `it is trained to aid a member of the Canadian Forces in carrying out that member’s duties`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "military animal means an animal that is trained to aid a member of the Canadian Forces in carrying out that member’s duties"

-- src:7807 | service animal means an animal that is required by a person with a disability for assistance and is certified, in writing, as having been trained by a professional service animal institution to assist a person with a disability. (animal d’assistance)
@ref s 445.01(4) "service animal" (src:7807-7807)
GIVEN `it is an animal that is required by a person with a disability for assistance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is certified, in writing, as having been trained by a professional service animal institution to assist a person with a disability` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 445.01(4) the animal is a service animal` MEANS
    IF `it is an animal that is required by a person with a disability for assistance` AND `it is certified, in writing, as having been trained by a professional service animal institution to assist a person with a disability`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "service animal means an animal that is required by a person with a disability for assistance and is certified, in writing, as having been trained by a professional service animal institution to assist a person with a disability"

-- 445.01 (1) Every one commits an offence who, wilfully and without lawful excuse, kills, maims, wounds, poisons or injures a law enforcement animal while it is aiding a law enforcement officer in carrying out that officer's duties,
-- a military animal while it is aiding a member of the Canadian Forces in carrying out that member's duties or a service animal.
-- src:7794 | Killing or injuring certain animals
-- src:7795 | 445.01 (1) Every one commits an offence who, wilfully and without lawful excuse, kills, maims, wounds, poisons or injures a law enforcement animal while it is aiding a law enforcement officer in carrying out that officer’s duties, a military animal while it is aiding a member of the Canadian Forces in carrying out that member’s duties or a service animal.
@ref s 445.01(1) (src:7794-7795)
GIVEN `the person acts wilfully` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acts without lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person kills, maims, wounds, poisons or injures the animal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the animal is a law enforcement animal, by s 445.01(4)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the animal is aiding a law enforcement officer in carrying out that officer’s duties` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the animal is a military animal, by s 445.01(4)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the animal is aiding a member of the Canadian Forces in carrying out that member’s duties` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the animal is a service animal, by s 445.01(4)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 445.01(1) the conduct is the offence of killing or injuring certain animals` MEANS
    IF `the person acts wilfully` AND `the person acts without lawful excuse` AND `the person kills, maims, wounds, poisons or injures the animal`
    THEN `ccc13 any of` (LIST `ccc13 all of` (LIST `the animal is a law enforcement animal, by s 445.01(4)`, JUST `the animal is aiding a law enforcement officer in carrying out that officer’s duties`)
                            , `ccc13 all of` (LIST `the animal is a military animal, by s 445.01(4)`, JUST `the animal is aiding a member of the Canadian Forces in carrying out that member’s duties`)
                            , `the animal is a service animal, by s 445.01(4)`)
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every one commits an offence who, wilfully and without lawful excuse, kills, maims, wounds, poisons or injures"

-- (2) (a) an indictable offence ... five years and, if a law enforcement animal is killed in the commission of the offence, to a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of six months; or (b) summary conviction and liable to a fine of not more than $10,000 or to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years less a day, or to both.
-- src:7796 | Punishment
-- src:7797 | (2) Every one who commits an offence under subsection (1) is guilty of
-- src:7798 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than five years and, if a law enforcement animal is killed in the commission of the offence, to a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of six months; or
-- src:7799 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction and liable to a fine of not more than $10,000 or to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years less a day, or to both.
@ref s 445.01(2) (src:7796-7799)
GIVEN `a law enforcement animal is killed in the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 445.01(2) the punishments` MEANS LIST
    (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `five years`, (IF `a law enforcement animal is killed in the commission of the offence` THEN `imprisonment for a term of` `six months` ELSE `no imprisonment is stated`), `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)   -- (a)
    , (Punishment OF `on summary conviction`, `imprisonment for a term of` `two years less a day`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `a fine of` 10000, `no fine is stated`)   -- (b)

@ref s 445.01(2) (the class of the offence) (src:7796-7799)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 445.01(2) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

-- (3) A sentence imposed on a person for an offence under subsection (1) committed against a law enforcement animal shall be served consecutively to any other punishment imposed on the person for an offence arising out of the same event or series of events.
-- The text names no one who must act, so no regulative rule is written (an actor is not invented): the decision function below says when the sentence is served consecutively.
-- src:7800 | Sentences to be served consecutively
-- src:7801 | (3) A sentence imposed on a person for an offence under subsection (1) committed against a law enforcement animal shall be served consecutively to any other punishment imposed on the person for an offence arising out of the same event or series of events.
@ref s 445.01(3) (src:7800-7801)
GIVEN `the sentence is imposed for an offence under subsection (1) committed against a law enforcement animal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other punishment is imposed on the person for an offence arising out of the same event or series of events` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 445.01(3) the sentence shall be served consecutively to the other punishment` MEANS
    IF NOT `the sentence is imposed for an offence under subsection (1) committed against a law enforcement animal`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A sentence imposed on a person for an offence under subsection (1) committed against a law enforcement animal"
    ELSE IF `the other punishment is imposed on the person for an offence arising out of the same event or series of events`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any other punishment imposed on the person for an offence arising out of the same event or series of events"

§§ `Cruelty to Animals -- sections 445.1 to 447.1`

-- 445.1 (1) Every one commits an offence who (a) wilfully causes or, being the owner, wilfully permits to be caused unnecessary pain, suffering or injury to an animal or a bird; (b) in any manner encourages, aids, promotes, arranges, assists at, receives money for or takes part in (i) the fighting or baiting of animals or birds, or (ii) the training, transporting or breeding of animals or birds for the purposes of subparagraph (i);
-- (c) wilfully, without reasonable excuse, administers a poisonous or an injurious drug or substance to a domestic animal or bird or an animal or a bird wild by nature that is kept in captivity or, being the owner ..., wilfully permits ...; (d) promotes, arranges, conducts, assists in, receives money for or takes part in any meeting, competition, exhibition, pastime, practice, display or event at or in the course of which captive birds are liberated ... for the purpose of being shot when they are liberated; or
-- (e) being the owner, occupier or person in charge of any premises, permits the premises or any part thereof to be used for a purpose mentioned in paragraph (d).
-- src:7809 | Cruelty to Animals
-- src:7810 | Causing unnecessary suffering
-- src:7811 | 445.1 (1) Every one commits an offence who
-- src:7812 | (a) wilfully causes or, being the owner, wilfully permits to be caused unnecessary pain, suffering or injury to an animal or a bird;
-- src:7813 | (b) in any manner encourages, aids, promotes, arranges, assists at, receives money for or takes part in
-- src:7814 | (i) the fighting or baiting of animals or birds, or
-- src:7815 | (ii) the training, transporting or breeding of animals or birds for the purposes of subparagraph (i);
-- src:7816 | (c) wilfully, without reasonable excuse, administers a poisonous or an injurious drug or substance to a domestic animal or bird or an animal or a bird wild by nature that is kept in captivity or, being the owner of such an animal or a bird, wilfully permits a poisonous or an injurious drug or substance to be administered to it;
-- src:7817 | (d) promotes, arranges, conducts, assists in, receives money for or takes part in any meeting, competition, exhibition, pastime, practice, display or event at or in the course of which captive birds are liberated by hand, trap, contrivance or any other means for the purpose of being shot when they are liberated; or
-- src:7818 | (e) being the owner, occupier or person in charge of any premises, permits the premises or any part thereof to be used for a purpose mentioned in paragraph (d).
@ref s 445.1(1) (src:7809-7818)
GIVEN `the person wilfully causes or, being the owner, wilfully permits to be caused unnecessary pain, suffering or injury to an animal or a bird` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person in any manner encourages, aids, promotes, arranges, assists at, receives money for or takes part in the fighting or baiting of animals or birds, or the training, transporting or breeding of animals or birds for those purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person wilfully, without reasonable excuse, administers, or, being the owner, wilfully permits to be administered, a poisonous or an injurious drug or substance to a domestic animal or bird or an animal or a bird wild by nature that is kept in captivity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person promotes, arranges, conducts, assists in, receives money for or takes part in any meeting, competition, exhibition, pastime, practice, display or event at or in the course of which captive birds are liberated for the purpose of being shot when they are liberated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person, being the owner, occupier or person in charge of any premises, permits the premises or any part thereof to be used for such a purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 445.1(1) the conduct is the offence of causing unnecessary suffering to animals` MEANS
    IF    `the person wilfully causes or, being the owner, wilfully permits to be caused unnecessary pain, suffering or injury to an animal or a bird`   -- (a)
       OR `the person in any manner encourages, aids, promotes, arranges, assists at, receives money for or takes part in the fighting or baiting of animals or birds, or the training, transporting or breeding of animals or birds for those purposes`   -- (b)
       OR `the person wilfully, without reasonable excuse, administers, or, being the owner, wilfully permits to be administered, a poisonous or an injurious drug or substance to a domestic animal or bird or an animal or a bird wild by nature that is kept in captivity`   -- (c)
       OR `the person promotes, arranges, conducts, assists in, receives money for or takes part in any meeting, competition, exhibition, pastime, practice, display or event at or in the course of which captive birds are liberated for the purpose of being shot when they are liberated`   -- (d)
       OR `the person, being the owner, occupier or person in charge of any premises, permits the premises or any part thereof to be used for such a purpose`   -- (e)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every one commits an offence who"

-- src:7819 | Punishment
-- src:7820 | (2) Every one who commits an offence under subsection (1) is guilty of
-- src:7821 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than five years; or
-- src:7822 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction and liable to a fine of not more than $10,000 or to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years less a day, or to both.
@ref s 445.1(2) (the punishments) (src:7819-7822)
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 445.1(2) the punishments` MEANS LIST
    (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `five years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)   -- limb 1: the limb the text states
    , (Punishment OF `on summary conviction`, `imprisonment for a term of` `two years less a day`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `a fine of` 10000, `no fine is stated`)   -- limb 2: the limb the text states

@ref s 445.1(2) (the class of the offence) (src:7819-7822)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 445.1(2) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

-- (3) For the purposes of proceedings under paragraph (1)(a), evidence that a person failed to exercise reasonable care or supervision of an animal or a bird thereby causing it pain, suffering or injury is, in the absence of any evidence to the contrary, proof that the pain, suffering or injury was caused or was permitted to be caused wilfully, as the case may be.
-- src:7823 | Failure to exercise reasonable care as evidence
-- src:7824 | (3) For the purposes of proceedings under paragraph (1)(a), evidence that a person failed to exercise reasonable care or supervision of an animal or a bird thereby causing it pain, suffering or injury is, in the absence of any evidence to the contrary, proof that the pain, suffering or injury was caused or was permitted to be caused wilfully, as the case may be.
@ref s 445.1(3) (src:7823-7824)
GIVEN `the proceedings are under paragraph (1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence that the person failed to exercise reasonable care or supervision of an animal or a bird thereby causing it pain, suffering or injury` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 445.1(3) the evidence is proof that the pain, suffering or injury was caused or permitted wilfully` MEANS
    IF NOT `the proceedings are under paragraph (1)(a)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "For the purposes of proceedings under paragraph (1)(a)"
    ELSE IF NOT `there is evidence that the person failed to exercise reasonable care or supervision of an animal or a bird thereby causing it pain, suffering or injury`
         THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection makes that evidence proof; where there is none it is silent
         ELSE IF `there is evidence to the contrary`
              THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the absence of any evidence to the contrary"
              ELSE JUST TRUE

-- (4) For the purpose of proceedings under paragraph (1)(b), evidence that an accused was present at the fighting or baiting of animals or birds is, in the absence of any evidence to the contrary, proof that he or she encouraged, aided or assisted at the fighting or baiting.
-- src:7825 | Presence at baiting as evidence
-- src:7826 | (4) For the purpose of proceedings under paragraph (1)(b), evidence that an accused was present at the fighting or baiting of animals or birds is, in the absence of any evidence to the contrary, proof that he or she encouraged, aided or assisted at the fighting or baiting.
@ref s 445.1(4) (src:7825-7826)
GIVEN `the proceedings are under paragraph (1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence that the accused was present at the fighting or baiting of animals or birds` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 445.1(4) the evidence is proof that the accused encouraged, aided or assisted at the fighting or baiting` MEANS
    IF NOT `the proceedings are under paragraph (1)(b)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "For the purpose of proceedings under paragraph (1)(b)"
    ELSE IF NOT `there is evidence that the accused was present at the fighting or baiting of animals or birds`
         THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection makes evidence of presence proof; where there is none it is silent
         ELSE IF `there is evidence to the contrary`
              THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the absence of any evidence to the contrary"
              ELSE JUST TRUE

-- 445.2 (1) In this section, cetacean includes any member of the cetacean order, including a whale, dolphin or porpoise.
-- src:7827 | Definition of cetacean
-- src:7828 | 445.2 (1) In this section, cetacean includes any member of the cetacean order, including a whale, dolphin or porpoise.
@ref s 445.2(1) (src:7827-7828)
GIVEN `it is a member of the cetacean order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a whale, dolphin or porpoise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 445.2(1) the animal is a cetacean` MEANS
    IF `it is a member of the cetacean order` OR `it is a whale, dolphin or porpoise`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "cetacean includes any member of the cetacean order"; the list is not closed

-- (2.1) If a cetacean is gestating on the day on which this subsection comes into force, paragraphs (2)(b) and (c) do not apply in respect of that cetacean for the period in which it gestates that includes the day on which this subsection comes into force.
-- src:7834 | Exception — gestation
-- src:7835 | (2.1) If a cetacean is gestating on the day on which this subsection comes into force, paragraphs (2)(b) and (c) do not apply in respect of that cetacean for the period in which it gestates that includes the day on which this subsection comes into force.
@ref s 445.2(2.1) (src:7834-7835)
DECLARE `s 445.2(2) paragraph` IS ONE OF
    `s 445.2(2)(a) owns, has the custody of or controls a cetacean that is kept in captivity`
    `s 445.2(2)(b) breeds or impregnates a cetacean`
    `s 445.2(2)(c) possesses or seeks to obtain reproductive materials of cetaceans, including sperm or an embryo`
    `s 445.2(2) no paragraph of subsection (2)`

@ref s 445.2(2.1) (src:7834-7835)
GIVEN paragraph IS A `s 445.2(2) paragraph`
      `the cetacean is gestating on the day on which subsection (2.1) comes into force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which subsection (2.1) comes into force` IS A DATE
      `the first day of the period in which it gestates that includes that day` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the period in which it gestates that includes that day` IS A DATE
      `the day of the act or omission` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 445.2(2.1) paragraphs (2)(b) and (c) do not apply in respect of the cetacean` MEANS
    IF NOT `the cetacean is gestating on the day on which subsection (2.1) comes into force`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a cetacean is gestating on the day on which this subsection comes into force"
    ELSE IF paragraph EQUALS `s 445.2(2)(a) owns, has the custody of or controls a cetacean that is kept in captivity` OR paragraph EQUALS `s 445.2(2) no paragraph of subsection (2)`
         THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "paragraphs (2)(b) and (c) do not apply"
         ELSE IF    Day `the day of the act or omission` AT LEAST Day `the first day of the period in which it gestates that includes that day`
                AND Day `the day of the act or omission` AT MOST Day `the last day of the period in which it gestates that includes that day`
                AND Day `the first day of the period in which it gestates that includes that day` AT MOST Day `the day on which subsection (2.1) comes into force`
                AND Day `the day on which subsection (2.1) comes into force` AT MOST Day `the last day of the period in which it gestates that includes that day`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for the period in which it gestates that includes the day on which this subsection comes into force"

-- (2.2) Paragraph (2)(a) does not apply to the offspring of a cetacean if that offspring was born immediately after a gestational period that included the day on which this subsection came into force.
-- src:7836 | Exception — offspring
-- src:7837 | (2.2) Paragraph (2)(a) does not apply to the offspring of a cetacean if that offspring was born immediately after a gestational period that included the day on which this subsection came into force.
@ref s 445.2(2.2) (src:7836-7837)
GIVEN `the animal is the offspring of a cetacean` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was born immediately after a gestational period that included the day on which subsection (2.2) came into force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 445.2(2.2) paragraph (2)(a) does not apply to the offspring of a cetacean` MEANS
    IF NOT `the animal is the offspring of a cetacean`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Paragraph (2)(a) does not apply to the offspring of a cetacean"; this subsection gives no exception on these facts (fork F12)
    ELSE IF `it was born immediately after a gestational period that included the day on which subsection (2.2) came into force`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if that offspring was born immediately after a gestational period that included the day on which this subsection came into force"

-- (3) Paragraph (2)(a) does not apply to a person who (a) owns, has the custody of or controls a cetacean that is kept in captivity at the coming into force of this section and remains continuously in captivity thereafter;
-- (b) has the custody of or controls a cetacean that is kept in captivity for the purpose of providing it with assistance or care or to rehabilitate it following an injury or another state of distress; or (c) is authorized to keep a cetacean in captivity ... pursuant to a licence issued by the Lieutenant Governor in Council of a province or by such other person or authority ...
-- src:7838 | Exception
-- src:7839 | (3) Paragraph (2)(a) does not apply to a person who
-- src:7840 | (a) owns, has the custody of or controls a cetacean that is kept in captivity at the coming into force of this section and remains continuously in captivity thereafter;
-- src:7841 | (b) has the custody of or controls a cetacean that is kept in captivity for the purpose of providing it with assistance or care or to rehabilitate it following an injury or another state of distress; or
-- src:7842 | (c) is authorized to keep a cetacean in captivity in the best interests of the cetacean’s welfare pursuant to a licence issued by the Lieutenant Governor in Council of a province or by such other person or authority in the province as may be specified by the Lieutenant Governor in Council.
@ref s 445.2(3) (src:7838-7842)
GIVEN `the person owns, has the custody of or controls a cetacean that is kept in captivity at the coming into force of section 445.2 and remains continuously in captivity thereafter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has the custody of or controls a cetacean that is kept in captivity for the purpose of providing it with assistance or care or to rehabilitate it following an injury or another state of distress` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is authorized to keep a cetacean in captivity in the best interests of the cetacean’s welfare pursuant to a licence issued by the Lieutenant Governor in Council of a province or by such other person or authority in the province as may be specified by the Lieutenant Governor in Council` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 445.2(3) paragraph (2)(a) does not apply to the person` MEANS
    IF `the person owns, has the custody of or controls a cetacean that is kept in captivity at the coming into force of section 445.2 and remains continuously in captivity thereafter` OR `the person has the custody of or controls a cetacean that is kept in captivity for the purpose of providing it with assistance or care or to rehabilitate it following an injury or another state of distress` OR `the person is authorized to keep a cetacean in captivity in the best interests of the cetacean’s welfare pursuant to a licence issued by the Lieutenant Governor in Council of a province or by such other person or authority in the province as may be specified by the Lieutenant Governor in Council`   -- (a), (b), (c)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Paragraph (2)(a) does not apply to a person who" is in one of the three cases; this subsection gives no exception on these facts (fork F12)

-- (3.1) Subsection (2) does not apply to a person who is conducting scientific research pursuant to a licence issued by the Lieutenant Governor in Council of a province or by such other person or authority in the province as may be specified by the Lieutenant Governor in Council.
-- src:7843 | Exception
-- src:7844 | (3.1) Subsection (2) does not apply to a person who is conducting scientific research pursuant to a licence issued by the Lieutenant Governor in Council of a province or by such other person or authority in the province as may be specified by the Lieutenant Governor in Council.
@ref s 445.2(3.1) (src:7843-7844)
GIVEN `the person is conducting scientific research pursuant to a licence issued by the Lieutenant Governor in Council of a province or by such other person or authority in the province as may be specified by the Lieutenant Governor in Council` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 445.2(3.1) subsection (2) does not apply to the person` MEANS
    IF `the person is conducting scientific research pursuant to a licence issued by the Lieutenant Governor in Council of a province or by such other person or authority in the province as may be specified by the Lieutenant Governor in Council`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (2) does not apply to a person who is conducting scientific research pursuant to a licence"; this subsection gives no exception on these facts (fork F12)

-- (2) Subject to subsections (2.1) to (3.1), every person commits an offence who (a) owns, has the custody of or controls a cetacean that is kept in captivity; (b) breeds or impregnates a cetacean; or (c) possesses or seeks to obtain reproductive materials of cetaceans, including sperm or an embryo.
-- src:7829 | Offence
-- src:7830 | (2) Subject to subsections (2.1) to (3.1), every person commits an offence who
-- src:7831 | (a) owns, has the custody of or controls a cetacean that is kept in captivity;
-- src:7832 | (b) breeds or impregnates a cetacean; or
-- src:7833 | (c) possesses or seeks to obtain reproductive materials of cetaceans, including sperm or an embryo.
@ref s 445.2(2) (src:7829-7833)
GIVEN `the animal is a cetacean, by s 445.2(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person owns, has the custody of or controls a cetacean that is kept in captivity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person breeds or impregnates a cetacean` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person possesses or seeks to obtain reproductive materials of cetaceans, including sperm or an embryo` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the exception of subsection (2.1) applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the exception of subsection (2.2) applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the exception of subsection (3) applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the exception of subsection (3.1) applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 445.2(2) the conduct is the offence of keeping, breeding or obtaining cetaceans` MEANS
    IF `the person owns, has the custody of or controls a cetacean that is kept in captivity` OR `the person breeds or impregnates a cetacean` OR `the person possesses or seeks to obtain reproductive materials of cetaceans, including sperm or an embryo`
    THEN `ccc13 all of` (LIST `the animal is a cetacean, by s 445.2(1)`
                            , `ccc13 any of` (LIST `ccc13 all of` (LIST JUST `the person owns, has the custody of or controls a cetacean that is kept in captivity`, `ccc13 not` `the exception of subsection (2.2) applies`, `ccc13 not` `the exception of subsection (3) applies`, `ccc13 not` `the exception of subsection (3.1) applies`)   -- (a)
                                                 , `ccc13 all of` (LIST JUST (`the person breeds or impregnates a cetacean` OR `the person possesses or seeks to obtain reproductive materials of cetaceans, including sperm or an embryo`), `ccc13 not` `the exception of subsection (2.1) applies`, `ccc13 not` `the exception of subsection (3.1) applies`)))   -- (b), (c)
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "every person commits an offence who"

-- (4) Every person commits an offence who promotes, arranges, conducts, assists in, receives money for or takes part in any meeting, competition, exhibition, pastime, practice, display or event at or in the course of which captive cetaceans are used, in Canada, for performance for entertainment purposes,
-- unless the performance is authorized under a licence issued by the Lieutenant Governor in Council of a province or by an authority in the province as may be specified by the Lieutenant Governor in Council. "unless" once met: JUST FALSE, fork F6.
-- src:7845 | Exception — authorization
-- src:7846 | (4) Every person commits an offence who promotes, arranges, conducts, assists in, receives money for or takes part in any meeting, competition, exhibition, pastime, practice, display or event at or in the course of which captive cetaceans are used, in Canada, for performance for entertainment purposes, unless the performance is authorized under a licence issued by the Lieutenant Governor in Council of a province or by an authority in the province as may be specified by the Lieutenant Governor in Council.
@ref s 445.2(4) (src:7845-7846)
GIVEN `the person promotes, arranges, conducts, assists in, receives money for or takes part in any meeting, competition, exhibition, pastime, practice, display or event` IS A BOOLEAN
      `captive cetaceans are used, in Canada, for performance for entertainment purposes at or in the course of it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the performance is authorized under a licence issued by the Lieutenant Governor in Council of a province or by an authority in the province as may be specified by the Lieutenant Governor in Council` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 445.2(4) the conduct is the offence of promoting a performance by captive cetaceans` MEANS
    IF `the performance is authorized under a licence issued by the Lieutenant Governor in Council of a province or by an authority in the province as may be specified by the Lieutenant Governor in Council`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the performance is authorized under a licence issued by the Lieutenant Governor in Council of a province"
    ELSE IF `the person promotes, arranges, conducts, assists in, receives money for or takes part in any meeting, competition, exhibition, pastime, practice, display or event` AND `captive cetaceans are used, in Canada, for performance for entertainment purposes at or in the course of it`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person commits an offence who promotes, arranges, conducts, assists in, receives money for or takes part in any meeting"

-- (5) Every one who commits an offence under subsection (2) or (4) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction and liable to a fine not exceeding $200,000.
-- src:7847 | Punishment
-- src:7848 | (5) Every one who commits an offence under subsection (2) or (4) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction and liable to a fine not exceeding $200,000.
@ref s 445.2(5) (src:7847-7848)
