`s 445.2(5) the punishments` MEANS LIST
    (Punishment OF `on summary conviction`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `a fine of` 200000, `no fine is stated`)

@ref s 445.2(5) (the class of the offence) (src:7847-7848)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 445.2(5) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence punishable on summary conviction`

-- 446 (1) Every one commits an offence who (a) by wilful neglect causes damage or injury to animals or birds while they are being driven or conveyed; or (b) being the owner or the person having the custody or control of a domestic animal or a bird or an animal or a bird wild by nature that is in captivity,
-- abandons it in distress or wilfully neglects or fails to provide suitable and adequate food, water, shelter and care for it.
-- src:7849 | Causing damage or injury
-- src:7850 | 446 (1) Every one commits an offence who
-- src:7851 | (a) by wilful neglect causes damage or injury to animals or birds while they are being driven or conveyed; or
-- src:7852 | (b) being the owner or the person having the custody or control of a domestic animal or a bird or an animal or a bird wild by nature that is in captivity, abandons it in distress or wilfully neglects or fails to provide suitable and adequate food, water, shelter and care for it.
@ref s 446(1) (src:7849-7852)
GIVEN `the person by wilful neglect causes damage or injury to animals or birds while they are being driven or conveyed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the owner or the person having the custody or control of a domestic animal or a bird or an animal or a bird wild by nature that is in captivity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person abandons it in distress or wilfully neglects or fails to provide suitable and adequate food, water, shelter and care for it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 446(1) the conduct is the offence of causing damage or injury to animals` MEANS
    IF `the person by wilful neglect causes damage or injury to animals or birds while they are being driven or conveyed` OR (`the person is the owner or the person having the custody or control of a domestic animal or a bird or an animal or a bird wild by nature that is in captivity` AND `the person abandons it in distress or wilfully neglects or fails to provide suitable and adequate food, water, shelter and care for it`)   -- (a), (b)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every one commits an offence who"

-- src:7853 | Punishment
-- src:7854 | (2) Every one who commits an offence under subsection (1) is guilty of
-- src:7855 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years; or
-- src:7856 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 446(2) (the punishments) (src:7853-7856)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 446(2) the punishments` MEANS LIST
    (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `two years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)   -- limb 1: the limb the text states
    , `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- limb 2: the text states no penalty: s 787(1)

@ref s 446(2) (the class of the offence) (src:7853-7856)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 446(2) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

-- src:7857 | Failure to exercise reasonable care as evidence
-- src:7858 | (3) For the purposes of proceedings under paragraph (1)(a), evidence that a person failed to exercise reasonable care or supervision of an animal or a bird thereby causing it damage or injury is, in the absence of any evidence to the contrary, proof that the damage or injury was caused by wilful neglect.
@ref s 446(3) (src:7857-7858)
GIVEN `the proceedings are under paragraph (1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence that the person failed to exercise reasonable care or supervision of an animal or a bird thereby causing it damage or injury` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 446(3) the evidence is proof that the damage or injury was caused by wilful neglect` MEANS
    IF NOT `the proceedings are under paragraph (1)(a)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "For the purposes of proceedings under paragraph (1)(a)"
    ELSE IF NOT `there is evidence that the person failed to exercise reasonable care or supervision of an animal or a bird thereby causing it damage or injury`
         THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection makes that evidence proof; where there is none it is silent
         ELSE IF `there is evidence to the contrary`
              THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the absence of any evidence to the contrary"
              ELSE JUST TRUE

-- 447 (1) Everyone commits an offence who builds, makes, maintains or keeps an arena for animal fighting on premises that he or she owns or occupies, or allows such an arena to be built, made, maintained or kept on such premises.
-- src:7859 | Arena for animal fighting
-- src:7860 | 447 (1) Everyone commits an offence who builds, makes, maintains or keeps an arena for animal fighting on premises that he or she owns or occupies, or allows such an arena to be built, made, maintained or kept on such premises.
@ref s 447(1) (src:7859-7860)
GIVEN `the person builds, makes, maintains or keeps an arena for animal fighting on premises that the person owns or occupies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person allows such an arena to be built, made, maintained or kept on such premises` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 447(1) the conduct is the offence of keeping an arena for animal fighting` MEANS
    IF `the person builds, makes, maintains or keeps an arena for animal fighting on premises that the person owns or occupies` OR `the person allows such an arena to be built, made, maintained or kept on such premises`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Everyone commits an offence who builds, makes, maintains or keeps an arena for animal fighting on premises that he or she owns or occupies"

