-- 447.1 (1) The court may, in addition to any other sentence that it may impose under subsection 445(2), 445.1(2), 446(2) or 447(2), (a) make an order prohibiting the accused from owning, having the custody or control of or residing in the same premises as an animal or a bird during any period
-- that the court considers appropriate but, in the case of a second or subsequent offence, for a minimum of five years; and (b) on application of the Attorney General or on its own motion, order that the accused pay to a person or an organization that has taken care of an animal or a bird as a result of the commission of the offence
-- the reasonable costs that the person or organization incurred in respect of the animal or bird, if the costs are readily ascertainable.
-- src:7866 | Order of prohibition or restitution
-- src:7867 | 447.1 (1) The court may, in addition to any other sentence that it may impose under subsection 445(2), 445.1(2), 446(2) or 447(2),
-- src:7868 | (a) make an order prohibiting the accused from owning, having the custody or control of or residing in the same premises as an animal or a bird during any period that the court considers appropriate but, in the case of a second or subsequent offence, for a minimum of five years; and
-- src:7869 | (b) on application of the Attorney General or on its own motion, order that the accused pay to a person or an organization that has taken care of an animal or a bird as a result of the commission of the offence the reasonable costs that the person or organization incurred in respect of the animal or bird, if the costs are readily ascertainable.
@ref s 447.1(1) (src:7866-7869)
GIVEN `the sentence for which the order is made` IS A `Provision of the Code`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 447.1(1)(a) the court may make an order prohibiting the accused from owning or having an animal or a bird` MEANS
    IF    (`the sentence for which the order is made`'s section EQUALS 445 AND `the sentence for which the order is made`'s subsection EQUALS "(2)")
       OR (`the sentence for which the order is made`'s section EQUALS 445.1 AND `the sentence for which the order is made`'s subsection EQUALS "(2)")
       OR (`the sentence for which the order is made`'s section EQUALS 446 AND `the sentence for which the order is made`'s subsection EQUALS "(2)")
       OR (`the sentence for which the order is made`'s section EQUALS 447 AND `the sentence for which the order is made`'s subsection EQUALS "(2)")
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in addition to any other sentence that it may impose under subsection 445(2), 445.1(2), 446(2) or 447(2)"

@ref s 447.1(1)(a) (the minimum period) (src:7868-7868)
GIVEN `the offence is a second or subsequent offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 447.1(1)(a) the prohibition must be for a minimum of five years` MEANS
    IF `the offence is a second or subsequent offence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the case of a second or subsequent offence, for a minimum of five years"

@ref s 447.1(1)(b) (src:7869-7869)
GIVEN `the sentence for which the order is made` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the Attorney General has applied or the court acts on its own motion` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payee is a person or an organization that has taken care of an animal or a bird as a result of the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the costs are readily ascertainable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 447.1(1)(b) the court may order the accused to pay the reasonable costs of taking care of the animal or bird` MEANS
    IF    (   (`the sentence for which the order is made`'s section EQUALS 445 AND `the sentence for which the order is made`'s subsection EQUALS "(2)")
           OR (`the sentence for which the order is made`'s section EQUALS 445.1 AND `the sentence for which the order is made`'s subsection EQUALS "(2)")
           OR (`the sentence for which the order is made`'s section EQUALS 446 AND `the sentence for which the order is made`'s subsection EQUALS "(2)")
           OR (`the sentence for which the order is made`'s section EQUALS 447 AND `the sentence for which the order is made`'s subsection EQUALS "(2)"))
      AND `the Attorney General has applied or the court acts on its own motion`
      AND `the payee is a person or an organization that has taken care of an animal or a bird as a result of the commission of the offence`
      AND `the costs are readily ascertainable`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the costs are readily ascertainable", on application or on the court's own motion, to a person or organization that has taken care of the animal or bird (fork F7)

DECLARE `s 447.1 act of the court` IS ONE OF
    `s 447.1(1)(a) make an order prohibiting the accused from owning, having the custody or control of or residing in the same premises as an animal or a bird`
    `s 447.1(1)(b) order the accused to pay the reasonable costs of taking care of the animal or bird`

@ref s 447.1(1)(a) (the power of the court) (src:7866-7868)
GIVEN `the court may make the order, by s 447.1(1)(a)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 447.1 act of the court`
`s 447.1(1)(a) the power of the court` MEANS
    IF `the court may make the order, by s 447.1(1)(a)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `the court` MAY `s 447.1(1)(a) make an order prohibiting the accused from owning, having the custody or control of or residing in the same premises as an animal or a bird`
    ELSE FULFILLED

@ref s 447.1(1)(b) (the power of the court) (src:7869-7869)
GIVEN `the court may make the order, by s 447.1(1)(b)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 447.1 act of the court`
`s 447.1(1)(b) the power of the court` MEANS
    IF `the court may make the order, by s 447.1(1)(b)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `the court` MAY `s 447.1(1)(b) order the accused to pay the reasonable costs of taking care of the animal or bird`
    ELSE FULFILLED

